================================================================================
3. GUARDRAIL MUTATION TESTING -- each behaviour broken, a test failed
================================================================================

The success metric requires the four guardrail behaviours be proven by
deliberately breaking each and confirming a test fails -- not by the suite
passing. Every mutation below was reverted immediately after its run
(`git checkout`); the tree carries none of them.

An important finding while doing this: implement and deploy are guarded by
THREE independent layers, not one --

  (i)   `providerOverrideEligible: false` in farm/steps_generated.json
  (ii)  their dispatch call sites in farm/step_agent.py never thread
        `provider=provider_override` at all
  (iii) `providerLocked: true`, enforced inside the real run_agent()

so a single-point flip of (i) alone is absorbed by (ii) and no test fails
(shown as 3c below, reported rather than hidden). That is defense in depth
working, not a missing test. To show the tests genuinely have teeth, each
layer is mutated in turn below and the failing test named.

